        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For a typical asphalt driveway in fair shape, doing the work yourself costs roughly a third to a half of a contractor bid, and the tools carry over to the next round. Hiring out earns its price on very large driveways, heavy crack repair, and for anyone who would rather not spend the weekend on it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Either way, the money that matters most goes into crack repair and a proper second coat, not into the most expensive pail on the shelf. Budget for sealing every two to three years, skip it on a driveway that is structurally failing, and compare contractor quotes line by line instead of by total.
          </p>
